      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(X>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
      "worked_solution": "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y<2) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,0),(1,1),(2,0),(2,1)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,0))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & \\,+P((X,Y)=(2,0))+P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & =f(1,0)+f(1,1)+f(2,0)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.05+0.15+0.05 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
